    "alpha_branch_artifact_note": "The RS ablation's R_allow(d) decays partly from a MEASUREMENT ARTIFACT: the FWER split alpha_branch = alpha_fwer/|N_d| shrinks as |N_d| grows, loosening each Clopper-Pearson lower bound and dragging R_allow toward 0 (e.g. OPA d=2 -> 0). The DETERMINISTIC Lipschitz backend has NO n_mc and NO alpha_branch, so its R_allow(d) decays only from the genuine min-over-more-branches effect and degrades more gracefully. Compare the two curves below.",
